{# THE ROSTER'S SHARED VOCABULARY — the marks every direction draws a person with.

   THE DESIGN UNROLLS THESE AND THIS DOES NOT, and that is the one deliberate
   difference between the two. In the workspace each direction is a standalone
   HTML file with every row written out, because a static page has no other way
   to be looked at; here six directions render the same twelve people, and six
   copies of "how a person is drawn" is six places for the tier pill to drift.

   The marks themselves are unchanged: same classes, same order, same words. A
   direction that wants a cell the others do not — b's band rows, f's department
   column — writes that itself and takes the rest from here.

   ICONS ARE INLINE LUCIDE SVGs, never emoji, and they live in macros for the
   same reason the cells do. #}

